! Bulk **rhombohedral** boron nitride (3R polytype, space group R3m) in its
! hexagonal setting: three layers and six atoms per cell, each layer slid by
! (1/3, 2/3) from the one below so that every boron sits over a nitrogen.
!
! Unlike the graphene and silicon cases this one is **polar**: R3m has no
! inversion centre, and `pw.x` finds 6 operations (C_3v) rather than 12. That is
! the reason the material is interesting here -- a non-centrosymmetric crystal
! has piezoelectricity as well as electrostriction, and the two are entangled in
! any measurement made by optimising under a finite field. The route P26 takes
! is immune to that: `d(chi)/d(strain)` at zero field is the electrostrictive
! response by construction (Tanner, Bousquet and Janolin, arXiv:2012.03841).
!
! `nosym`/`noinv` with an **unshifted** grid, for the reason every case in this
! family carries: the object being differentiated has a field label and a strain
! label at once, and no rank-3 average is written for it, so the k-set has to be
! closed under the point group rather than reduced.
!
! The lattice constants are the measured ones (a = 2.504 A, c = 9.99 A), not a
! relaxed geometry, so there is a residual stress; `vdw_corr` is on because the
! interlayer binding is van der Waals and PBE alone does not have it.
!
! **This grid is not converged and the header of any result must say so.** 2x2x2
! is the smallest closed grid there is; see PLAN.md P28 for the convergence
! study and for what a comparison with a measurement actually needs.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 4, celldm(1) = 4.73175, celldm(3) = 3.98946, nat = 6, ntyp = 2,
    ecutwfc = 80.0
    occupations = 'fixed'
    nosym = .true.
    noinv = .true.
    vdw_corr = 'grimme-d2'
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-12
    mixing_beta = 0.7
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 B  10.811  B.pbe-hgh.UPF
 N  14.007  N.pbe-hgh.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (crystal)
 B 0.000000000000 0.000000000000 0.000000000000
 N 0.333333333333 0.666666666667 0.000000000000
 B 0.333333333333 0.666666666667 0.333333333333
 N 0.666666666667 0.333333333333 0.333333333333
 B 0.666666666667 0.333333333333 0.666666666667
 N 0.000000000000 0.000000000000 0.666666666667
K_POINTS (automatic)
 2 2 2 0 0 0
